foreign  welcome to another installment of Harry  Potter Theory today we're going to be  discussing curses more specifically  we're going to be taking a look at 10 of  the worst cruelest most intense dark  curses in The Wizarding World and  putting them in order I'm going to be  going into what they are and why I  placed them where I did first things  first what is a curse and how does it  differ from say a spell charm Jinx or  hex as far as these categories of magic  go curses most closely resemble charms a  charm is an expression that refers two  spells which adds certain properties to  objects or individuals jobs should not  be confused with transfigurations as  Transfiguration refers to a spell that  changes what the object is rather than  just changing properties of the object  there are countless charms in Harry  Potter that cover all manner of outcomes  there are also different types of charms  another form of charm is an enchantment  though the lines were a bit blurred here  the main difference is that an  enchantment is generally used to apply a  charm-like effect to something for an  extended period of time these would  include protective enchantments like the  videlius charm or protego Maxima and  with the definition of charm solidified  the easiest way to describe a curse is  that it's a dark charm technically a  curse is defined as any spell that  affects an object in a negative manner  typically causing some sort of pain or  discomfort and just like charms there  are also more acute short-lived versions  of curses that contrast the more  stretched out Affliction type curses  within the Potter World the boundaries  are flexible and I imagine Wizards may  have their own ideas this shows that the  categorization of dark charms is not set  in stone and may sometimes be used  interchangeably this explains why some  spells are known by multiple names like  why the slug vomiting charm is a curse  and while the jelly legs curse is also  sometimes known as the jelly legs jinx  this also explains why some curses such  as the leg Locker curse jelly legs curse  and full body bind curse which don't  cause an elasting injury seem to fall  more under the definition of a jinx or  hex while Voldemort's Jinx on the post  of defense against the dark arts teacher  has had serious lasting consequences for  several of those affected which would  seem more like a curse this list will  include both types of curses before we  get started pause the video and comment  your list of what you believe to be the  most horrible curses in Harry Potter I  did a lot of rearranging while working  on this video and I think I'm happy with  how it turned out let's get into it 10.  gormleth gaunts curse what starting  things off this curse produced by Irish  pure-blooded dark witch gormlath gaunt  and of his old Sayer had the ability to  place someone into an enchanted Slumber  you might be thinking that's not so bad  I can get to bed a little easier but the  strength of this curse is what makes it  dangerous this curse is sort of  reminiscent of the one that Afflicted  Snow White  why here this spell certainly deserves  to be on the list but not any higher  than the bottom placing I say this  because the curse itself is relatively  painless and doesn't pose any  significant risk to your mortality the  curse also can be broken if the stimulus  around the victim is significant enough  9. imperious curse the imperious curse  AKA imperio is one of the three  unforgivable curses imperio is most  often used by dark witches and wizards  and when it is cast on a victim they are  forced to perform the unquestioned  bidding of the Caster being under the  control of this spell is said to be like  experiencing a wonderful release from  any sense of responsibility making the  victim extremely susceptible to any sort  of influence from the Caster because of  this adopted Carefree attitude the  victim is inclined to carry out tasks  for the Caster without any sort of moral  comfort office or awareness of the  Caster's intentions or desires why here  I placed the imperial's curse fairly low  on the list because at the end of the  day being placed under the imperious  curse is not a death sentence  furthermore it's been emphasized in the  books that being under the imperial's  curse can actually provide the victim  with some temporary relief from the  stresses of life it was the most  wonderful feeling Harry felt a floating  sensation as every thought in worry in  his head was wiped gently away leaving  nothing but a vague untraceable  happiness the more I think about it the  imperious curse could actually be a  positive and useful tool in the right  hands with just the swish of your wand  you'd be able to give your friends  family members some temporary relief in  the darker times during their lives to  some simply numbing the pain may not be  an advisable strategy but that certainly  depends on the person eight lycanthropy  lycanthropy is a magical condition that  transforms witches Wizards into  werewolves one who suffers from this  condition is called a lycanthrope there  are two ways to become a lycanthrope but  regardless of how it is contracted it is  still considered to be a curse that will  completely alter the victim's existence  the first way to contract lycanthropy is  through being bitten by a werewolf  though in some circumstances the bite  can will kill you the second way is via  the lycacomia curse which apparently  requires nowhere Wolves at all why here  though inheriting lycanthropy doesn't  kill you and to some the prospect of  becoming a werewolf may be exciting I  can assure you that it is no easy  existence the stigma in The Wizarding  World surrounding werewolves is immense  and from the moment you can track this  curse it's unlikely that you will ever  be treated the same furthermore  lycanthropes will often need to live a  very solitary lonely existence as  allowing people to become close to you  only puts their lives in danger this  awful condition also has no cure 7. opal  necklace curse when Harry mistakenly  enters borgenberg's 1992 he sees a  necklace on display with a warning label  do not touch cursed has claimed the  lives of 19 muggle owners to date this  necklace was of course the opal necklace  the same cursed object that Katie Bell  fell victim to in the Half-Blood Prince  It's untelling what cursed the opal  necklace actually possesses but we do  know that it can cause some serious  damage to those who happen to come into  physical contact with it Katie Millie  touched it through a small hole in her  glove and it took her six months to  recover in Saint mungo's why here this  curse is nothing to scoff at but at the  end of the day there are much worse  curses out there yeah it's highly lethal  but touching it is not necessarily A  death sentence and it's also pretty easy  to avoid 6. curse on marvelo gone to  ring the curse on Marvel gaunts ring was  an invention of Lord Voldemort who  created it in an effort to protect his  horcruxes Dumbledore famously contracts  this curse when he places the cursed  ring on his finger in that moment  securing his Fate The Curse is thought  to be extremely deadly ticking down even  Dumbledore and the only reason that he  was able to survive as long as he did  was with the help of Severus Snape the  symptoms of the curse mimic necrosis  slowly turning the affected areas black  and effectively killing that part of  your body why here I think this  placement on the list is suitable as the  curses effectively a slightly worse  version of The Curse contracted via the  opal necklace the main difference here  being that this curse will eventually  kill you and only seems to get worse  over time  5. blood malediction maledictus a  maledictus curse is applied to and  inherited through a witch or Wizard's  bloodline a dark curse that is passed on  through generations of family members  and is transferred from mother to  daughter a maledictus suffers from a  blood malediction a type of curse that  causes the sufferer to slowly transform  into an animal over the course of their  life the animal can vary according to  the specific curse in Harry Potter the  main maledictus that comes to mind is  nagini whose blood malediction meant  that she was destined to turn into a  snake becoming less human and more Snake  each and every day in early life the  maledictus will possess the ability to  transform it well but that's what slips  over time eventually you will lose the  ability to transform and will be stuck  in whatever animal form that is destined  for you why here though blood  malediction doesn't kill you it's an  Affliction that leads to a very isolated  lonely existence it's an awful curse  that you're born with and have no way  out of it's an inescapable curse that  eats away at you slowly stripping away  your identity I imagine that suffering  from this curse would induce a form of  claustrophobia as with each passing day  the curse goes stronger further trapping  you into a permanent animal state if  that isn't bad enough once fully  transformed you completely lose the  ability to explain yourself or  communicate with your own kind  4. killing curse the killing curse  otherwise known as Avada Kedavra is a  curse that kills the victim in the blink  of an eye causing instantaneous death if  you want to kill someone with no fuss  then this is certainly the spell to use  after uttering the incantation the spell  produces a blindingly intense green bolt  of light right before the victim simply  drops dead there are two theories for  how they die the first claiming that the  victim's internal organs cease to  function after being struck and the  second claiming that the soul of the  victim is magically ripped from their  body  why here the only reason that the  killing curse isn't higher on the list  is that we're lacking information if the  curse does indeed rip the soul out of  the body then perhaps the killing curse  is one of the worst ways to die however  if it simply causes your organs to shut  down then this is potentially one of the  more remorseful ways to kill people as  they are gone instantly with no  suffering to speak of 3. entrail  expelling curse the entrail expelling  curse is fairly self-explanatory it's a  curse that forces your entrails insides  organs to be magically expelled ripped  from the body this curse is  unquestionably lethal why here this  curse kills you fairly brutally which is  why it's high up on a list however there  are no real drawn out torturous effects  2. cruciatus curse the cruciatus curse  otherwise known as crucio is one of the  Unforgivable curses in essence grusio is  the spell used for torture which makes  perfect sense if we consider that crucio  translates to my torture in Latin when  cast crucio inflicts excruciating pain  on the victim pain so excruciating that  it is considered to be torturous casting  crucio is said to require a wand and  incantation and its effects are said to  vary depending on the Caster's desires  and emotions to produce the excruciating  pain implied by the name the Caster must  despise the victim and enjoy causing  pain Harry Potter after crucia was cast  on him described it as feeling like his  head was being split open while having  his bones set on fire why here there are  a few reasons for why crucio is so high  up on the list the first reason being  that the pain induced to Via crucio is  said to be so excruciating that in some  cases death would be preferable the next  reason is that crucio when applied to a  victim for long enough is said to cause  permanent effects like brain damage this  happened to Neville Longbottom's parents  after being tortured relentlessly the  long bottoms lost everything that made  them who they were living out the rest  of their lives as broken Shadows of  their former selves this Bell is  particularly awful if we consider the  fact that the loved ones of these  victims will forever have to witness  them in this state all while knowing  that they were tortured in their final  moments 1. transmography and torture oh  boy where do I start with this one this  sadistic curse that a lot of you may not  know about effectively combines the  effects of crucio with a form of  transmogrification or Transfiguration  this terrible curse does indeed kill its  victims but not before causing them  intense torturous pain stretched out of  a considerable period of time why here  if we look at the etymology of the  cursor's name which features  transmogrify it would suggest that the  curse stretches the victim in a  multitude of directions  grotesquely contorting their bodies  until they die the combination of the  fact that this spell is lethal and  tortures you in unprecedented ways makes  this an easy choice for the List's top  spawns why this isn't an unforgivable  curse when it features aspects from two  of the existing unforgivable curses is  beyond me and that's it for this video  which curses had you heard of was your  list similar to mine leave a comment  down below until next time remember it  does not do to dwell on dreams and  forget to live  [Music]

